# Local Claude Code settings override — a daemon clone on a host without the operator's own global gitignore
# must not read as dirty just because this per-host file exists (ruling clause 3(iv): a daemon refuses to
# rebuild over an unsafe/dirty tree, and this file is host-local noise, never tracked content).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Progress-board GENERATED output (item x9t5i5a) — the page is re-derived from
# reports/progress-board.json plus live `gh` state on every run, so committing it would churn the tree on
# every refresh (the timestamp alone changes each time) with nothing a reader could review. The cache
# sidecar is the last good `gh` snapshot, machine-local, safe to lose — it only exists so a rate-limited or
# offline run still renders a page. The hand-maintained state file itself IS tracked.
reports/progress-board.html
reports/.progress-board-cache.json

# Required-status-checks GENERATED cache (#2748 false-red follow-up, we:scripts/lib/required-status-checks.mjs)
# — same shape as the progress-board cache above: the last good `gh api .../protection` read, machine-local,
# safe to lose (a stale or missing cache just falls back to a fresh live fetch or the hardcoded fallback set).
reports/.required-status-checks-cache.json

# Decision Docket GENERATED HTML (backlog/3562's data/template separation, scripts/gen-decision-docket.mjs)
# — same shape as progress-board above: the page is a PURE re-render of reports/decision-docket-data.json
# through skills-src/decision-docket/template.html, so committing it would churn the tree every run (the
# generatedAt timestamp alone) with nothing a reader could review in the diff. The DATA file is the thing
# meant to be tracked — its git history is the real, diff-able "what changed and when" record this rebuild
# exists to provide, replacing the hand-written "Correction —"/"second pass" prose the old process baked
# into the page itself. Regenerate the page any time with `npm run gen:decision-docket`.
reports/decision-docket.html

# Parcel build cache (trait-enforcer #787 conformance harness)
.parcel-cache/

# Build sourcemaps (emitted alongside compiled output, never committed)
*.js.map
*.d.ts.map

# Publish-built compiled output emitted next to sources in package planes (#2085)
# — these packages ship .ts sources directly (contracts/package.json files: ['*.ts'])
contracts/**/*.js
contracts/**/*.d.ts
capability-manifest/**/*.js
capability-manifest/**/*.d.ts
error-summary/**/*.js
error-summary/**/*.d.ts
commitment-policy/**/*.js
commitment-policy/**/*.d.ts
.claude/lane-ports.json
# Nothing under .conveyor/ is ever tracked — it is all daemon/session state. A daemon clone must never
# read dirty from its own state (2026-09-24 freeze: an untracked `.conveyor/unsupported-repo.json` made a
# live daemon clone's tree look dirty and its rebuild/self-sync refused). This directory-wide rule is kept
# alongside the older individual `.conveyor/*` entries below rather than replacing them, since those carry
# their own incident history.
.conveyor/
# Delivery-agent learnings drop-box (#2614) — transient per-session capture (like claims.json). Agents
# append generalized-lesson entries during a session; the /closing-session sweep consumes it at close. Never
# committed — it holds pre-vetting, pre-dedup entries that the sweep + red-team curate before anything lands.
.conveyor/learnings/
# A resident daemon's own stdout/stderr log (e.g. review-daemon.mjs, pass-daemon.mjs, launchd's
# StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath target) — machine-local operational output, never committed. Live-caught
# 2026-09-22, #xvyuwtg: an ungitignored `.conveyor/review-daemon.log` made a dedicated daemon clone look
# permanently DIRTY to git, which blocks that checkout's own staleness auto-fast-forward
# (scripts/lib/main-staleness.mjs's `cleanOnly` auto-ff requires a clean tree) — the daemon's own routine
# operation was silently defeating its own recovery path.
.conveyor/*.log
# Session-local conveyor CLEAR-FOR-BUILD queue (#2613) — the operator's "clear this item for the conveyor
# to pull" gesture. Session-local operator INTENT, not committed repo state (distinct from committed
# `buildQueued` frontmatter), so it rides a gitignored sidecar the lane guard does not police — that is what
# lets the operator clear work from the MAIN session (see scripts/conveyor/queue.mjs). Never committed.
.conveyor/queue.json
# Dispatch-signal sidecar (#2680) — the ephemeral "small signal, not a durable store" that makes conveyor
# authoring measurable (dispatch → first-commit stamps the `gh`/backlog verbs cannot see). Machine-local,
# recreated on demand by `conveyor-instrument.mjs mark-dispatch`/`mark-setup`; never committed, like queue.json.
.conveyor/dispatch-log.json
# Session-local conveyor INFRA-BLOCKED state (#2659) — a delivery/prepare agent that PUSHED its lane ref but
# hit a PR-open failure on an outside dependency (a GitHub outage) records the resumable handle here; the
# conveyor auto-retries + resume-opens once infra recovers. Operational recovery state, never committed.
.conveyor/infra-blocked.json
# …and (epic #3383) the re-nag dedup record + human log for its own "surfaced past the attempt cap, needs a
# human" escalation (`planSurfaceEscalation`) — same per-checkout, machine-disposable state as the
# driver-watchdog's own alert/log pair just below, never committed.
.conveyor/infra-blocked-alert.json
.conveyor/infra-blocked.log
# Unsupported-repo durable-owed-work sidecar (`scripts/conveyor/unsupported-repo.mjs`) — written by
# `runReconcileFixDispatch`/`runner.mjs` EVERY tick (even to record "nothing outstanding"), same as every other
# `.conveyor/*.json` marker here. Never gitignored until #3383 (epic #3383's own red-main incident): the SAME
# failure mode `.conveyor/*.log` above was added for on 2026-09-22 (#xvyuwtg) — an ungitignored per-tick sidecar
# reads as a permanently DIRTY tree, which blocks a dedicated daemon clone's self-sync (`daemon-self-sync.mjs`'s
# `decideSelfSync` fails closed on `dirty`, forever, even once `origin/main` moves) exactly like the earlier one
# blocked `main-staleness.mjs`'s auto-fast-forward. Machine-local, recreated on demand; never committed.
.conveyor/unsupported-repo.json
# CI queue-wait history sidecar (#3574) — the periodic `gh run list` wait-time sample the resident runner's own
# tick appends to, so a genuine Actions run-queue regression becomes a visible trend instead of invisible.
# Machine-local, recreated on demand by ci-queue-watch.mjs sweep; never committed, like the other sidecars here.
.conveyor/ci-queue-history.json
# False-green evidence sidecar (#2681) — the diff-driven test-selection shadow full-suite compare records each
# sample (was a full-suite failure OUTSIDE the shrink's selected set?) here. Ephemeral measure-mode evidence the
# eventual default-on decision reads; machine/CI-local, recreated on demand, never committed.
.conveyor/false-green-log.json
# Red-main dispatch-freeze marker (#2681) — present ⇒ the sole writer STOPS THE LINE (main is red). Operational
# stop-the-line state raised/lifted by red-main-remediation.mjs; machine-local, never committed.
.conveyor/red-main-freeze.json
# Manual/emergency dispatch-pause marker (#3609) — present ⇒ dispatch-plan.mjs and tick-core.mjs hold every
# otherwise-launchable item/spawn `dispatch-paused`, without touching already-running lanes. Operator-set/cleared
# via dispatch-pause.mjs set|clear; machine-local advisory state, never committed.
.conveyor/dispatch-pause.json
# Queue-scoped mechanical passes marker (epic #3383) — present+true ⇒ this checkout's repo-wide passes
# (reconcile/review-dispatch, the three open-PR watch sweeps, verify-dispatch) act ONLY on PRs/lanes its own
# .conveyor/queue.json names. Absent ⇒ today's repo-wide default. Set/cleared via queue-scope.mjs set|clear;
# machine-local and instance-local by construction, never committed.
.conveyor/queue-scope.json
# Driver-watchdog state (epic #3383) — the EXPLICITLY-recorded fallback commit a silently-stale driver is rolled
# back to (`last-known-good.json`, written by `driver-watchdog.mjs record-good` before the driver is promoted
# onto new code), the re-nag dedup record for its escalation (`watchdog-alert.json`), and its human log. All
# three are per-checkout state about a LOCAL process — machine-disposable (memory rule 105), never committed.
.conveyor/last-known-good.json
.conveyor/watchdog-alert.json
.conveyor/watchdog.log
# …and the LAUNCH-POSTURE marker the runner writes at its own startup (epic #3383) — `resident` (keep driving
# until stopped) vs `bounded` (`--once` / `--max-ticks=N`: run N ticks and exit). Without it the watchdog cannot
# tell a bounded driver that FINISHED from a resident one that CRASHED — both are "no lease" — and it reported
# the finish as a crash every 5 minutes. Same nature as the three above: per-checkout facts about a LOCAL
# process, machine-disposable (memory rule 105), never committed.
.conveyor/driver-mode.json
# The promotion trail that WRITES that fallback (epic #3383) — `validate-and-promote.mjs` appends one line per
# pass (validated / refused / promoted / no-op) into the DRIVER's own checkout, beside the watchdog's log. Same
# nature: a record of what a LOCAL process did to a LOCAL checkout, machine-disposable, never committed.
.conveyor/promote.log
# …and its advisory lock (serializes concurrent record/retry writes) — ephemeral (created+unlinked per
# critical section), but ignore it so a crashed holder's leftover lock never shows as an untracked file.
.conveyor/*.lock
# Durable append-only JURY event log (#2641) — one .jsonl per review subject; the review pipeline appends events
# and the shared fold (we:scripts/lib/jury-ledger.mjs) reconstructs the live jury tree the conveyor + #2642
# console render. Operational observability state (the #2612 single source of truth), machine-local, never committed.
.conveyor/jury/
# Durable EXTERNAL driver-status file (#3521/lane-2 incident, 2026-09-14) — the headless runner's own
# self-diagnosed per-tick status (statusLine, stalled items, dispatch), overwritten every tick so a SEPARATE
# process (a human, another agent, `scripts/conveyor/driver-status.mjs`) can answer "is the driver stuck?"
# without grepping runner.log. Machine-local, recreated every tick, never committed.
.conveyor/driver-status.json
# Day-sharded plain-language DECISION TRACE (#3521 decision-trace v1, 2026-09-14) — one JSONL file per day, one
# line per dispatch/skip/stall decision the driver made and WHY, appended every tick. Operational observability
# state (mirrors the `.operations/telemetry/<date>.jsonl` day-sharding convention), machine-local, never committed.
.conveyor/decision-trace/
# Live-toggleable driver-verbose marker (#3521 decision-trace v1 follow-up, 2026-09-14) — set/cleared via
# `driver-verbose.mjs on|off`, re-read (and its bounded `--ticks=N` window advanced) every tick by the currently
# running driver. Session-local advisory state, never committed, like every other `.conveyor/*.json` marker here.
.conveyor/driver-verbose.json
# Durable per-fork MICRO-DECISION log (#2665) — one .jsonl per review subject; the read port appends a record
# per human action on a fork (challenge/ask/annotate) and the surface fold reconstructs it, mirroring the jury
# sidecar above. Operational state (machine-local), recreated on demand, never committed.
.conveyor/micro-decisions/
# Per-session runtime bookkeeping (TTL'd, machine-local) — tooling recreates on demand (#952).
# SoT relocated to skills-src/ (#2266), so ignore the real path; capacity.json is durable calibration → stays tracked.
skills-src/batch-backlog-items/claims.json
skills-src/batch-backlog-items/queued.json
skills-src/batch-backlog-items/reservations.json
skills-src/batch-backlog-items/prepare-hold.json
skills-src/batch-backlog-items/id-ledger.json
# Review-escalation park-age clock (#2262) — local, machine-scoped, safe to lose (a PR just re-parks fresh)
# Both the built skill dir and the skills-src/ source dir the drain writes from (the source path leaked to the primary).
.claude/skills/drain/review-park-state.json
skills-src/drain/review-park-state.json
# First-drain-sighting manifest baseline (#2414) — same machine-scoped, safe-to-lose cache as the park-age
# clock above, and same skills-src/ source-path leak. Untracked → dirtied the daemon clone every pass, firing a
# false "recovering from interrupted pass" reset; ignoring it also lets the tamper baseline persist cross-pass.
.claude/skills/drain/review-baseline-state.json
skills-src/drain/review-baseline-state.json
# Operation-engine RUN RECORDS (#3032, epic #3029) — one JSON file per in-flight run of a declared
# operation. A half-finished run is transient operator/session intent, not durable repo readiness, so it
# rides a gitignored sidecar the card-mutation guard does not police (clause 1 of
# docs/agent/platform-decisions.md#state-lives-where-its-nature-dictates), exactly like .conveyor/queue.json.
# NOT the verdict ledger (#3007) — that is the durable merge authority and a different object entirely; see
# scripts/operations/run-record.mjs. Never committed.
.operations/
# `check:health`'s report — recomputed fresh from current backlog state on every run (its own source
# comment already disclaims it: "regenerable tool output, not a /research/ deliverable"). Was tracked, so
# any lane that ran the close-out gate's diagnostic mode was left permanently dirty (`git status --porcelain`
# gates lane-pool recycling), starving the lane pool (#1153 hit this before). Nobody reads the committed
# copy as source of truth — every workflow reference re-runs the command. Generate on demand instead.
audits/backlog-health-audit.md
# The run-scorecard store's OLD home (#4155). It was git-tracked, so every review round's codex advisory seat
# (#3907) appending a row dirtied the review-daemon clone, its self-sync refused to move it, the clone fell
# behind main and every review dispatch refused as stale. The store now lives outside every checkout
# (scripts/conveyor/run-scorecard-store.mjs#resolveScorecardStorePath) and migrates this file's history there;
# ignoring the path keeps a copy an older process still writes from ever dirtying a checkout again.
scripts/conveyor/run-scorecards.json
# #4077 health watch state (episodes, per-daemon memory, last-tick stamp) — local state under the pinned state
# root, never committed; the plist example points CONVEYOR_STATE_ROOT at the operator's own checkout.
.conveyor/health/

# Fixer before/after evidence scratch — never committed; post it as a PR comment
/.fix-evidence*.md
/.fix-*-evidence*.md
